Broccoli Phillips 2018; Shi 2024; UC Davis Three independent source records
Tomato Phillips 2018 (vitamin C); separate carotenoid source Nutrient-specific records

One species is not one observation, and one publication is not necessarily one independent experiment. Study identity, sample identity, and independence are preserved as first-class attributes.

9.4 Acceptance criteria and scope

The pilot is accepted when, for every record: verifiable replay succeeds; normalized replay succeeds within \epsilon; no dimensional violation occurs; provenance reaches a source entity; the separation invariant holds; and the three assessment structures are reported separately. Records with \mathsf{Miss} states are included; the pipeline is judged on their correct handling, not on their exclusion.

The pilot is not powered for H1. Three sampling occasions per season are far below the per-group size implied by the TOST formula for any plausible \Delta and \sigma. The sampling-season proposition is descriptive, not inferential in the §7.1 sense. This is a limitation of evidential reach, and it should be stated plainly rather than obscured by a “seasonality” heading.

---

10. Discussion

10.1 What survives independently of empirical outcome

If H1 and H3 are rejected or left unresolved, the framework retains value as a provenance-preserving, replayable infrastructure that keeps four seasonality dimensions distinct and records the epistemic status of every claim. The primary contribution is architectural and methodological, not empirical.

10.2 Limitations

Institutional calendar coverage is incomplete and heterogeneous. WorldCereal's global calendars cover maize and wheat and map temporary crops; they do not cover perennials such as orange or most horticultural species, and MIRCA lumps vegetables into “Others annual.” The horticultural calendar gap is therefore larger than a passing limitation, and the Atlas must either source national calendars or model horticultural windows from remote sensing and station data.

WCVP covers vascular plants only. Fungi and fish, both strongly seasonal, require a second taxonomic authority and an explicit crosswalk. This is a scope limitation, not a detail.

No single vocabulary is universally applied across FAO, EuroFIR, and USDA, so the harmonization layer constructs its own alignments with explicit versioning. Published seasonal-variation studies are small and rarely control for cultivar, maturity, storage, and method, which constrains identifiability and motivates the unresolved classification. Conversion factors for fresh-to-dry basis are frequently undocumented in secondary records, which is why basis transformation is gated on a documented moisture measurement and cultivar-independence.

The name “FoodAtlas” is already in use for a UC Davis knowledge graph linking foods, chemicals, diseases, and flavour descriptors through provenance-tracked edges. The present system should be renamed or explicitly positioned against that work rather than colliding with it.

10.3 The durability argument

A research infrastructure should survive criticism of its own foundations. The framework therefore separates what is established from what is proposed, states its non-claims explicitly, and makes each formal guarantee conditional on named hypotheses that can be tested and, if necessary, refuted. This is the condition under which a later researcher can inspect the Atlas without having to trust its authors' intentions.

---

11. Conclusion

The Atlas is specified as a typed observation algebra with a provenance-preserving harmonization layer. Four seasonality domains are represented as distinct mathematical objects with a partial-identification relation between them, not a false claim of non-recoverability. Missing information is represented through typed measurement states with a partial arithmetic whose defensible property is closure—non-numeric states never become numeric—rather than a universal no-silent-zero claim. Reconstruction is established as verifiable replay under stated hypotheses, not as universal invertibility. Non-loss attaches to the augmented archival representation with well-defined locators, not to normalized values alone. Consistency is established as conditional confluence on a restricted domain, not as unconditional commutation. Quality and evidence are separated into three independently reported structures without claiming statistical independence. H1 and H3 are formulated with explicit estimands, environmental covariates, censoring-aware likelihoods, effect-size anchors, and a four-category inferential classification rebuilt from equivalence bounds; H2 is descoped rather than asserted.

The framework makes no empirical assertion about the healthfulness or sustainability of seasonal food. It constructs the conditions under which such assertions can be tested, audited, corrected, and, where necessary, refuted.


