The append-only event model matches the PROV-O versioning pattern: a mutable resource is connected to immutable revision entities, rather than mutated in place. This alignment is architectural, not merely nominal: the framework's replay semantics and PROV-O's entity/activity distinction are the same distinction between a payload and the process that produced it.

H.6 METROFOOD-IT integrity alignment

METROFOOD-IT uses selective, hash-only on-chain anchoring. Only cryptographic hashes of selected assets are recorded on the ledger, while full datasets remain off-chain. The framework aligns by anchoring Merkle roots of record batches, not individual records:

· Each batch of records produces a Merkle tree over canonical serialisations.
· The Merkle root is anchored on-chain.
· Individual records and their events remain off-chain.
· Verification recomputes the Merkle path from the record to the anchored root.

This preserves the cost and privacy properties of the METROFOOD-IT architecture and makes the framework interoperable with it.

